1
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:15,830
Yesterday,

2
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,550
you were so full of yourself

3
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,800
when you smashed my goods.

4
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:23,230
What?

5
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,160
Today, you're here asking for help?

6
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,390
Fine.

7
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:31,510
We've known each other for many years.

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,350
=Cases Between Us=
I will help you.

9
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:34,750
But I have

10
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:35,920
one condition.

11
00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:38,080
=Episode 34=
One favor

12
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:39,240
for one question.

13
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:49,030
Yesterday, you smashed this vase

14
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,520
and said it was fake.

15
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:53,320
Today, in front of everyone,

16
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:57,430
I'd like you to judge it again.

17
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,350
You want the truth?

18
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,040
I want to hear

19
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,710
whatever you choose to say.

20
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:20,560
It's genuine.

21
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:22,790
What?

22
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:25,350
Isn't this the same vase from yesterday?

23
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,280
Young Master Zhao, he...

24
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:29,840
It's genuine?

25
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:32,870
But you said it was fake.

26
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,120
Take another look.

27
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,920
No need.

28
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:37,430
It's genuine.

29
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,350
Young Master Zhao,

30
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,590
I thought you never got it wrong.

31
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:46,230
It's obviously a fake.

32
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:47,840
How did you come to that conclusion?

33
00:01:48,096 --> 00:01:49,232
How about this one?

34
00:01:51,430 --> 00:01:54,510
Go on.

35
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:58,350
It's genuine.

36
00:01:58,710 --> 00:01:59,480
Wrong.

37
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:01,710
It's fake.

38
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:11,080
If you keep passing off
fakes as genuine,

39
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:13,630
how are you ever going to survive
in Liulichang Antique Market?

40
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:19,430
My knowledge is shallow.

41
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:21,870
I'm shortsighted.

42
00:02:23,856 --> 00:02:25,710
I've been talking nonsense
about every piece

43
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:27,296
that has passed through my hands.

44
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,030
My apologies.

45
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,190
Apologies?

46
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:39,680
Just flapping your gums is enough?

47
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,150
Well, well.

48
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,150
You've been standing
on your high horse for too long.

49
00:03:08,310 --> 00:03:09,520
Is that really

50
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:11,470
how you ask someone for a favor?

51
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:19,590
Walk out that door,

52
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,800
and you'll never know

53
00:03:21,984 --> 00:03:23,520
where those imperial antiques went.

54
00:03:31,310 --> 00:03:32,150
Come on.

55
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,160
Young Master Zhao.

56
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,870
You really know how
to swallow your pride.

57
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,750
But you're thinking too simply.

58
00:05:02,976 --> 00:05:05,024
Liulichang Antique Market
isn't the only place

59
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:08,040
that deals in antiques.

60
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:11,430
What are you getting at?

61
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:12,950
Like I said,

62
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,480
one favor,

63
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,870
one question.

64
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,680
What more do you want?

65
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:34,830
Still got some backbone, huh?

66
00:05:35,510 --> 00:05:36,680
He actually came.

67
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:45,920
Young Master Zhao,

68
00:05:46,870 --> 00:05:47,920
if you can take

69
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:51,000
these eight welcoming rods

70
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:54,120
and crawl to my feet,

71
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,800
I'll count that

72
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,000
as your second favor.

73
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:04,270
What?

74
00:06:04,430 --> 00:06:05,190
Lost your nerve?

75
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:06,720
If you're scared, go home.

76
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:08,310
Right!

77
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:09,240
- Go home!
- Go home!

78
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,360
Young Master Zhao.

79
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:12,950
Afraid?

80
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,870
If this is all the sincerity you've got.

81
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,360
Show him out.

82
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,720
- Go home!
- Go home!

83
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,680
I told you.

84
00:06:25,750 --> 00:06:26,630
He chickened out.

85
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,480
What a waste of time.

86
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,560
He knelt.

87
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:37,720
This rascal.

88
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:07,390
Hit him harder.

89
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:09,950
Young Master Zhao has thick skin.

90
00:07:09,950 --> 00:07:10,920
Right, everyone?

91
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:11,870
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

92
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:13,070
- Harder!
- Harder!

93
00:07:41,430 --> 00:07:42,920
He's coughing up blood.

94
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:44,360
He's bleeding.

95
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,830
Everyone.

96
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,120
Take a good look.

97
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:52,360
This is Young Master Zhao who once
ruled Liulichang Antique Market.

98
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,360
Look at him now.

99
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:58,630
How is he any different from a stray dog?

100
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:01,600
- Exactly!
- He's a stray.

101
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,310
Look at him.

102
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:37,910
Good for him.

103
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
He really took it.

104
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:39,750
Right.

105
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:40,750
I didn't expect that.

106
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,656
- He held on.
- He held on.

107
00:08:42,850 --> 00:08:43,620
He really did.

108
00:08:53,232 --> 00:08:54,150
Young Master Zhao.

109
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,790
Closer.

110
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:12,200
To be honest,

111
00:09:14,030 --> 00:09:15,000
I never

112
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,000
realized that

113
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,720
you had

114
00:09:20,544 --> 00:09:21,480
such backbone.

115
00:09:23,390 --> 00:09:24,360
But your knees

116
00:09:25,550 --> 00:09:26,550
are pretty soft.

117
00:09:26,550 --> 00:09:27,240
Wouldn't you say?

118
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:28,820
- That's right.
- That's right.

119
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,750
You're too naive.

120
00:09:36,030 --> 00:09:38,320
I only said you could ask.

121
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:42,390
I never said I would answer.

122
00:09:42,910 --> 00:09:43,870
Isn't that right,

123
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:44,750
everyone?

124
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,240
- That's right.
- That's right!

125
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:48,200
Exactly, he never said that.

126
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:00,750
Nice!

127
00:10:01,030 --> 00:10:01,840
This feels great!

128
00:10:02,896 --> 00:10:04,240
Let's go and have some tea.

129
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:05,600
Let's go.

130
00:10:05,670 --> 00:10:06,720
Come on.

131
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:07,790
Move.

132
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:13,260
(Pleasures of Pottery and Fishing)

133
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,550
Stop.

134
00:11:20,030 --> 00:11:21,630
Isn't this Young Master Zhao?

135
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:24,240
Have a rough day?

136
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,670
Si, give Young Master Zhao a hand.

137
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:31,670
Master Liang,

138
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:33,550
good day.

139
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:37,750
You look to be

140
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:40,630
in high spirits today.

141
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,000
Young Master Zhao,

142
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,440
that's not quite fair.

143
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:46,510
Back then, when you ruined
other people's business

144
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:47,360
and embarrassed them,

145
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:49,510
weren't you just riding the tide, too?

146
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,440
You can't blame me
just because the wind has changed

147
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:55,030
and you've fallen from your pedestal.

148
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,080
Since you know the wind can change,

149
00:12:00,790 --> 00:12:02,150
you also know

150
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,120
it begins with the slightest breeze.

151
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,200
East wind or west,

152
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,240
who knows

153
00:12:09,024 --> 00:12:10,480
which way it will blow tomorrow?

154
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,550
Young Master Zhao,

155
00:12:13,030 --> 00:12:15,910
do you know why,
of all the spoiled rich guys in Beijing,

156
00:12:16,150 --> 00:12:19,440
I like you the most?

157
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:24,670
Because you see things clearly.

158
00:12:26,030 --> 00:12:27,030
You're right.

159
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:29,120
Once the wind changes,

160
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,360
no one knows where it will blow.

161
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:33,790
That's why I never corner people.

162
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,030
I came today to tell you this.

163
00:12:37,030 --> 00:12:42,030
You won't find those imperial antiques
in Liulichang Antique Market.

164
00:12:46,750 --> 00:12:47,360
What...

165
00:12:47,870 --> 00:12:48,720
What do you mean?

166
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,720
I'm a man

167
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,670
who appreciates atmosphere.

168
00:12:57,550 --> 00:13:00,720
Nothing beats a lone fortress

169
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:03,240
against the setting sun.

170
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:05,910
If you want the best view

171
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:07,790
in Beijing,

172
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:12,600
go to the old watchtower
at the Weng City.

173
00:13:14,150 --> 00:13:15,030
Young Master Zhao,

174
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,750
if you're in the mood tonight,

175
00:13:16,750 --> 00:13:18,240
take a walk up there.

176
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:19,790
You might see

177
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,240
something worth seeing.

178
00:13:25,510 --> 00:13:26,910
Since when are you this kind?

179
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,790
I have parents to care for

180
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:35,750
and children to raise.

181
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:40,120
Seeing how desperate you are
to save your father,

182
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:42,000
I couldn't help but feel for you.

183
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:46,030
Think of it as earning a little virtue.

184
00:13:46,510 --> 00:13:49,670
Believe me or not, that's up to you.

185
00:14:02,870 --> 00:14:04,720
Funny world, isn't it?

186
00:14:05,670 --> 00:14:08,510
Today it's the east wind.
Tomorrow, the west.

187
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:10,480
Yet, somehow the wind

188
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,320
never blows my way.

189
00:14:12,544 --> 00:14:14,512
That's because
you're good at playing the game.

190
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:18,600
In this life,

191
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:20,600
people chase fame,

192
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,670
fortune,

193
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,600
honor,

194
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:24,910
or love.

195
00:14:26,390 --> 00:14:27,360
Try to have them all,

196
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:30,120
and you'll end up with none.

197
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:34,440
There's a blade
beside the character "profit."

198
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:40,550
It cuts down those blinded by greed.

199
00:14:47,870 --> 00:14:48,480
Yang,

200
00:14:48,896 --> 00:14:51,000
how many years
have you been with the department?

201
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,270
Commissioner,

202
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,360
eight years.

203
00:14:57,150 --> 00:14:58,870
Before Yuan Hong left,

204
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:01,030
he specifically recommended you.

205
00:15:01,030 --> 00:15:01,870
Do you know

206
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:03,670
why I only made you

207
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:05,030
acting chief?

208
00:15:08,870 --> 00:15:10,670
The key to being an official

209
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:13,720
is knowing the ropes.

210
00:15:14,030 --> 00:15:15,240
When to reach out

211
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,840
and when to stay well away,

212
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:18,840
you need to be clear.

213
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,870
You may not understand that yet.

214
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,000
That's alright.

215
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,240
As for the rest,

216
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:27,550
it depends on how quickly you learn.

217
00:15:49,790 --> 00:15:52,320
♪Good folks♪

218
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:54,150
♪Bad folks♪

219
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:57,670
♪None should wear the begonia♪

220
00:15:57,740 --> 00:16:02,860
(Serve the People
with Loyalty and Integrity)

221
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,120
- Get to work!
- Move!

222
00:16:15,510 --> 00:16:16,200
Who are you?

223
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,120
Lost your mind?

224
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,240
Zhao?

225
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:24,840
What happened to you?

226
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:27,120
Do me a favor.

227
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:44,200
I really can't help

228
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:47,320
with your father's case.

229
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:49,080
He was framed.

230
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,510
Those missing imperial antiques

231
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,480
still haven't surfaced on the market.

232
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:54,600
Tonight,

233
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:57,360
a shipment of antiques
is being moved through the city gate.

234
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,960
I think something's off.

235
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,320
I need to borrow a few men

236
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,792
to come with me to the watchtower.

237
00:17:13,440 --> 00:17:15,680
The Commissioner
has been watching me like a hawk.

238
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,590
He just lectured me,

239
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,030
saying he'd be observing my performance.

240
00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:37,640
Fine.

241
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:40,680
Thanks.

242
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:42,960
Hold on.

243
00:17:55,952 --> 00:17:57,216
How many men do you need?

244
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:03,510
Two plainclothes teams...

245
00:18:05,270 --> 00:18:06,830
Shouldn't we report this to...

246
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:18,510
Buddy,

247
00:18:18,510 --> 00:18:19,510
let's go.

248
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,424
I'll help you, even if I lose my job.

249
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:29,340
(End of Episode 34)

250
00:18:29,801 --> 00:18:31,441
♪Side by side,
we journey through this life♪

251
00:18:31,441 --> 00:18:32,981
♪Troubled times
are but a laughing matter♪

252
00:18:32,981 --> 00:18:34,231
♪However, the world changes♪

253
00:18:34,231 --> 00:18:36,151
♪You'll still be by my side♪

254
00:18:36,151 --> 00:18:37,841
♪Side by side,
we journey through this life♪

255
00:18:37,841 --> 00:18:39,411
♪Praise and blame come and go♪

256
00:18:39,411 --> 00:18:40,981
♪If this is my final chapter♪

257
00:18:40,981 --> 00:18:43,481
♪I'll solve this mystery with you♪
